From 44865f82d616d9bbc8faaa74f9db12c1a67b2b90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:08:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 124/138] RAM tier: drop a turn's superseded tail checkpoint
 once its own new tail is stored

An agent turn resumes from the previous turn's tail checkpoint (one row per
offloaded group) and stores its own, later one; the old rows can then only
serve a request ending exactly there, and filled the tier until evicted.
OffloadingManager.discard() frees idle keys (stores/loads in flight are kept);
the scheduler records each request's resume boundary and attaches the old
tail's keys to the new tail's store job, discarding them after the store has
completed on every worker unless another live request shares that prefix or
the keys are being loaded. VLLM_OFFLOAD_DISCARD_SUPERSEDED=0 disables it.
Counter kv_offload_discarded_rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
